```mermaid
classDiagram
    %% Subsystem Class Diagram: Browser + WebRTC + Signaling + Media Server + Processing
    class Browser {
      +getUserMedia()
      +createPeerConnection()
      +addTrack()
      +sendSignaling(msg)
    }

    class RTCPeerConnection
    class MediaStream
    class AudioTrack
    class VideoTrack
    class OpusEncoder
    class VP8Encoder
    class WebSocketSignaling
    class FastAPI_Signaling
    class aiortc_Peer
    class MediaProcessor
    class SFU
    class SFU_Worker
    class Recorder
    class EventBus

    Browser --> RTCPeerConnection : creates
    RTCPeerConnection o-- MediaStream : has
    MediaStream o-- AudioTrack : contains
    MediaStream o-- VideoTrack : contains
    AudioTrack --> OpusEncoder : encoded by
    VideoTrack --> VP8Encoder : encoded by
    RTCPeerConnection --> WebSocketSignaling : uses
    WebSocketSignaling --> FastAPI_Signaling : forwards
    FastAPI_Signaling --> aiortc_Peer : negotiates (SDP/ICE)
    aiortc_Peer --> MediaProcessor : delivers frames for processing
    aiortc_Peer <.. SFU : alternative connection
    SFU --> SFU_Worker : distributes streams
    SFU_Worker --> MediaProcessor : subscribes
    MediaProcessor --> Recorder : optional persistent storage
    MediaProcessor --> EventBus : publishes events (transcripts, detections)
    EventBus --> Browser : push events to UI

    %% Notes
    note for OpusEncoder "Opus (RTP) — WebRTC audio codec"
    note for aiortc_Peer "aiortc runs on Python backend — receives RTP, exposes tracks"
```
